# External reference repositories

Before inventing significant new subsystem mechanics, read:

- [docs/MASTER_BLUEPRINT.md](docs/MASTER_BLUEPRINT.md)
- [docs/PRODUCT_SPEC.md](docs/PRODUCT_SPEC.md)
- [docs/CURRENT_STATE_AUDIT.md](docs/CURRENT_STATE_AUDIT.md)
- [docs/EXTERNAL_REFERENCE_REPOS.md](docs/EXTERNAL_REFERENCE_REPOS.md)

Select references **by subsystem** from that registry. Inspect **no more than 3** external repositories by default. Never analyze every registered repo on every task.

Prefer proven implementations/patterns over unnecessary greenfield reinvention. Reuse existing local code before importing external patterns. A listed repo does **not** mean we must adopt it.

This repository remains authoritative. Local canonical docs override external examples. Never wholesale-merge an external application. Never replace our Supabase/RLS model, four commercial truths, verification/provenance, human-final pricing, `L&P INPUT REQUIRED`, purpose-aware retrieval, or canonical UX/IA.

Never copy source without checking the repository’s **current** LICENSE. AGPL / non-permissive / unlicensed / unclear projects are **reference-only** unless explicitly approved. Record material upstream research lazily under `docs/reference-repos/` (see that folder’s README). Do not clone external repos into this project.
